;; The mini-playground, second version (RFC-041): the first plan's six stages,
;; then a Chat section and a modern UI shell — a menu, one section at a time,
;; terminal and editor tabs, a theme. Mode A: brainyard's root agent builds
;; each bead. plan2-claude.edn is mode B, the same stages and checks.
;;
;;   jolt sim:byj dev/sim/playground/plan2.edn --score
;;   jolt sim:byj compare RUN-A RUN-B
;;
;; The backlog fixes the conventions the checks rely on, as a person's spec
;; would; the agents choose everything else. No browser here: the UI checks
;; read the hooks the spec names, from the page and its scripts.
{:id "playground2"
 :projects-dir "~/Projects/byj-sim"
 :provider "claude-code" :model "sonnet"
 :permission-mode :auto
 :timeout-s 1800
 :cap-usd 12.0
 :stage-cap-usd 2.0
 :answers [{:match "pkill" :answer "n"}]
 :default-answer "n"
 :stages
 [{:id :init
   :lines ["/init"
           "This project is a mini-playground: a small web workspace. Stack: Node 20+, a plain node:http server with ws and node-pty, a static page using xterm.js, tests with node --test. Conventions: npm start runs the server on the port in PORT (default 3000); npm test runs the tests, which must not depend on port 3000 being free (another server may hold it) — when you start the server yourself, give it another port. File each of these as a bead, in order, each depending on the one before: (1) server shell: a page with a sidebar of sections Terminal, Files, Editor and Chat, GET /api/health answering {\"ok\":true}, and 404 for unknown paths; (2) a terminal over a WebSocket at /term spawning $SHELL in the project dir, with JSON frames {\"t\":\"i\",\"d\":text} from the client and {\"t\":\"o\",\"d\":text} from the server, the shell killed when the socket closes; (3) a {\"t\":\"r\",\"cols\":n,\"rows\":n} frame resizes the shell, and a client connecting to /term?id=<id> with an id used before is replayed that terminal's recent output; (4) the Terminal section in the page: xterm.js loaded from the server, the fit addon, and a status badge element with a data-status attribute (connecting, open, reconnecting, closed); (5) a file tree and a text editor: GET /api/files?path= lists a directory, GET /api/file?path= answers a file's text and PUT /api/file?path= writes the request body, the file's text as it is, and any path outside the project dir is answered 400; (6) a Chat section (data-section=\"chat\"): POST /api/chat with JSON {\"message\":text} answers a text/event-stream of data: lines and ends with event: done, from a pluggable backend whose default echoes the message back; the page shows the conversation and reads the stream as it comes; (7) a modern UI shell: a top bar with a menu (role=\"menubar\") for the sections; only the current section shown, switched by the URL hash, the others hidden; tabs (role=\"tablist\", each role=\"tab\") for several terminals, each tab with data-term-id and its own /term?id=, and a + button (data-action=\"new-terminal\") that opens another; tabs for the files open in the editor, each with data-file; a dark/light theme toggle (data-action=\"toggle-theme\") switching data-theme on the html element, remembered in localStorage; and a layout that works on a narrow screen (@media). Don't start building yet."]
   :checks [{:type :file :name "agents-md" :path "AGENTS.md" :contains "BRAINYARD:project"}
            {:type :command :name "seven-beads" :run "test $(bd list --all 2>/dev/null | grep -c '^[○◐✓]') -ge 7"}]}
  {:id :server
   :lines ["Work on the next ready bead (bd ready): build it, make its tests pass, commit, and close the bead."]
   :checks [{:type :command :name "npm-test" :run "npm test" :timeout-s 300}
            {:type :command :name "health" :run "node {{plan}}/checks/checks.cjs health" :timeout-s 90}]}
  {:id :term
   :lines ["Work on the next ready bead (bd ready): build it, make its tests pass, commit, and close the bead."]
   :checks [{:type :command :name "npm-test" :run "npm test" :timeout-s 300}
            {:type :command :name "term" :run "node {{plan}}/checks/checks.cjs term" :timeout-s 90}]}
  {:id :resize
   :lines ["Work on the next ready bead (bd ready): build it, make its tests pass, commit, and close the bead."]
   :checks [{:type :command :name "npm-test" :run "npm test" :timeout-s 300}
            {:type :command :name "resize" :run "node {{plan}}/checks/checks.cjs resize" :timeout-s 90}]}
  {:id :ui
   :lines ["Work on the next ready bead (bd ready): build it, make its tests pass, commit, and close the bead."]
   :checks [{:type :command :name "npm-test" :run "npm test" :timeout-s 300}
            {:type :command :name "ui" :run "node {{plan}}/checks/checks.cjs ui" :timeout-s 90}]}
  {:id :files
   :lines ["Work on the next ready bead (bd ready): build it, make its tests pass, commit, and close the bead."]
   :checks [{:type :command :name "npm-test" :run "npm test" :timeout-s 300}
            {:type :command :name "files" :run "node {{plan}}/checks/checks.cjs files" :timeout-s 90}]}
  {:id :chat
   :lines ["Work on the next ready bead (bd ready): build it, make its tests pass, commit, and close the bead."]
   :checks [{:type :command :name "npm-test" :run "npm test" :timeout-s 300}
            {:type :command :name "chat" :run "node {{plan}}/checks/checks.cjs chat" :timeout-s 90}]}
  {:id :shell
   :lines ["Work on the next ready bead (bd ready): build it, make its tests pass, commit, and close the bead."]
   :checks [{:type :command :name "npm-test" :run "npm test" :timeout-s 300}
            {:type :command :name "shell" :run "node {{plan}}/checks/checks.cjs shell" :timeout-s 90}]}]}
